menu "BoardSim Wi-Fi"

    config BOARDSIM_WIFI
        bool "Emulate Wi-Fi when running in BoardSim"
        default y
        select ETH_USE_OPENETH
        help
            In BoardSim (QEMU) there is no radio. With this on, the esp_wifi API
            is emulated on top of the emulated Ethernet: connecting succeeds,
            the usual Wi-Fi and IP events arrive on the station interface, and
            QEMU's NAT gives the firmware network and internet access through
            the computer. On real hardware every call goes to ESP-IDF's own
            Wi-Fi unchanged; the check is made at run time.

    config BOARDSIM_WIFI_AUTOCONNECT
        bool "Connect as soon as Wi-Fi is started"
        default y
        depends on BOARDSIM_WIFI
        help
            In BoardSim, act as if esp_wifi_connect() was called when the
            station starts, so firmware that waits for saved credentials still
            gets a network. Off: only esp_wifi_connect() connects.

    config BOARDSIM_WIFI_SSID
        string "Network name reported in BoardSim"
        default "BoardSim"
        depends on BOARDSIM_WIFI

endmenu
